# Secrets: never bake them into an image (the ** forms also cover swatchroom/.env and swatchroom/keys/)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/service-account*.json
**/catalogue-signer*.json
**/modal-service-account*.json
**/*-key.json
**/credentials/
**/keys/
.git
**/node_modules
tests/e2e/node_modules
_legacy_python_site
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.venv
models/
.cache/
data/
# Local test output of the Design Studio's browser walk-throughs
swatchroom/tests/shots-*
swatchroom/tests/sa.json
# The catalogue engine (catalogue/) runs on Modal or on your own computer, never in the website's image; the notebook it came from does not belong in it either
catalogue/
**/*.ipynb
# The built site is made inside the image (Dockerfile: RUN node tools/build-dist.js); a copy built on this computer would be stale or from another version
dist/
# The designer's hand-off of the landing page (65 MB, mostly full-size picture sources): the website serves site/landing/, which is built from it
Terucon_landingPage_2/
